import Surreal.HahnSeries.BoundedOrbitLocus
import Surreal.HahnSeries.MvComposition
import Surreal.HahnSeries.PolynomialFactorLifting

/-!
# Exact multipliers and finite-parameter Hahn evaluation

This file formalizes `epd:prop:multiplier` and `epd:lem:evaluation` of
`docs/surcomplex/expanding-polynomial-dynamics/article.tex`, in the Hahn workspace
`K = k⟦Γ⟧` with valuation `v = orderTop` (so `v(0) = ⊤`), integral ring
`𝒪 = nonnegativeSubring Γ k` and residue map `st = standardPart Γ k`.

## Composite polynomials

`iterateComp f n` is the `n`-fold composite polynomial `f ∘ ⋯ ∘ f` (with `f^{∘0} = X`) over any
commutative ring. `eval_iterateComp` identifies its evaluation with the `n`-th iterate of
evaluation, and `eval_derivative_iterateComp` is the chain rule for formal derivatives,
`(f^{∘n})'(x) = ∏_{j < n} f'(f^j(x))`. `eval_derivative_iterateComp_add` splits it as
`(f^{∘(m+p)})'(x) = (f^{∘m})'(x) · (f^{∘p})'(f^m(x))`.

## `epd:prop:multiplier`

For `P ∈ 𝒪[X]` and `q ∈ K`, `forwardPoly P q = C q⁻¹ * P` is the polynomial `F = q⁻¹ P`, whose
evaluation is `Surreal.BranchMetric.forwardMap P q` (`eval_forwardPoly`), and
`iteratePoly P q n` is the composite polynomial `Fⁿ`, differentiated formally in `X`
(primes hold the coefficients fixed, as in the source).

* `orderTop_eval_derivative_forwardPoly`: at `y ∈ 𝒪` with `P̄'(st y) ≠ 0`,
  `v(F'(y)) = -κ` where `κ = v(q)`.
* `isRoot_map_standardPart`: if `y ∈ 𝒪`, `F(y) ∈ 𝒪` and `v(q) = κ > 0`, then
  `P(y) = q F(y) ∈ 𝔪`, so `st y` is a root of `P̄`. This is the itinerary step of the source.
* `orderTop_eval_derivative_iteratePoly` is clause (1) for any `P ∈ 𝒪[X]` all of whose residue
  roots are simple: `v((Fⁿ)'(x)) = -nκ` for `x ∈ B_int(F)` and every `n` (including `n = 0`).
* `mem_integralLocus_of_iterate_eq`: if `F^{m+p}(x) = F^m(x)` with `p ≥ 1`, then
  `x ∈ B_int(F)`, provided `deg P ≥ 2` and the leading coefficient of `P` is a unit. The source
  quotes this from `epd:thm:periodic`; here it is derived directly from the escape step
  (`Surreal.ValuedIteration.iterate_add_ne_of_neg`), since every iterate of a preperiodic point
  is preperiodic.
* `orderTop_eval_derivative_preperiodic` is the valuation computation behind clause (2). It
  holds at every `x ∈ B_int(F)`, root or not: for `m ≥ 0` and `p ≥ 1`, the derivative of
  `F^{m+p}(X) - F^m(X)` at `x` has valuation `-(m + p)κ`, through the source's factorization
  `(F^m)'(x) ((F^p)'(F^m(x)) - 1)`.
* `preperiodic_root` is clause (2): every root `x ∈ K` of `F^{m+p}(X) - F^m(X)` lies in
  `B_int(F)`, so the derivative there has valuation `-(m + p)κ`, and
  `rootMultiplicity_eq_one_of_orderTop` turns this into simplicity of the root (root
  multiplicity exactly `1` in `K[X]`). Only roots lying in `K` are addressed: the statement
  does not say that the polynomial splits over `K` or is squarefree over an algebraic closure.
  The source reads "at a root" as "at every root" because `epd:thm:periodic` (not formalized
  here) shows that the polynomial has `d^{m+p}` distinct roots, all in `K`.
* `multiplier_integral` and `multiplier` state the proposition for the family
  `epd:eq:polynomial`, `P = a ∏ (X - c_i) + ∑_{j ≤ d} e_j X^j` with `a ≠ 0`, distinct `c_i`,
  `e_j ∈ 𝔪`, `q ∈ 𝔪 \ {0}` and `κ = v(q)`; clause (1) does not use `d ≥ 2`, clause (2) does.
  `simpleRoots_perturbedPolynomial` records that every residue root of this `P` is simple.

## `epd:lem:evaluation`

Write the source's parameters `a_1, …, a_r` as `x : σ → K` (the Lean argument names). The strong
evaluation `A ↦ A(x)` is `Surreal.HahnSeries.mvEvaluate x hx`, a `k`-algebra homomorphism
`k[[Z_1, …, Z_r]] →ₐ[k] K` by construction; this clause of the lemma is carried by the type of
`mvEvaluate`, not by a separate conjunct. `evaluation` packages the remaining clauses for inputs
`x : σ → K` in `𝔪` (zero inputs allowed, `σ` finite): the family `A_d x^d` is strongly summable
with sum `A(x)`; `A(x) ∈ 𝒪`; the support of `A(x)` lies in the additive monoid generated by the
input supports; evaluation respects formal substitution by zero-constant series; and the ideal
clause. The ideal clause is the new statement `mvEvaluateNonnegative_mem_span`: if
`A ∈ (Z_j : j ∈ J)` then `A(x) ∈ (x_j : j ∈ J) 𝒪`, for any set `J` of parameter indices.

Generality: `k` is an arbitrary field (the source takes `ℝ` or `ℂ`) and `Γ` is any linearly
ordered abelian group; neither `Γ ≠ 0` nor divisibility is used. No hypothesis beyond the
source's is added. No clause of `epd:prop:multiplier` or `epd:lem:evaluation` is pending, with
clause (2) of `epd:prop:multiplier` read for roots in `K` as explained above; the splitting of
`F^{m+p}(X) - F^m(X)` over `K` and the count `d^{m+p}` belong to `epd:thm:periodic`.
-/

namespace Surreal.ExpandingMultipliers

open Polynomial
open scoped _root_.HahnSeries
open _root_.HahnSeries (addVal addVal_apply SummableFamily)
open Surreal.HahnSeries
open Surreal.BranchMetric (forwardMap forwardMap_coe perturbedPolynomial residuePolynomial
  map_perturbedPolynomial eval_derivative_residuePolynomial_ne_zero
  orderTop_eq_zero_of_standardPart_ne_zero standardPart_eq_zero_of_orderTop_pos
  natDegree_perturbedPolynomial isUnit_leadingCoeff_perturbedPolynomial)
open Surreal.ValuedIteration (integralLocus mem_integralLocus mem_integralLocus_hahn
  isExpanding_hahn iterate_add_ne_of_neg forwardMap_eq)

noncomputable section

/-! ### Composite polynomials and the chain rule -/

section Chain

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The `n`-fold composite polynomial `f^{∘n} = f ∘ ⋯ ∘ f`, with `f^{∘0} = X`. -/
def iterateComp (f : R[X]) (n : ℕ) : R[X] :=
  f.comp^[n] X

theorem iterateComp_zero (f : R[X]) : iterateComp f 0 = X :=
  rfl

theorem iterateComp_succ (f : R[X]) (n : ℕ) :
    iterateComp f (n + 1) = f.comp (iterateComp f n) :=
  Function.iterate_succ_apply' _ _ _

/-- Evaluating the composite polynomial iterates evaluation. -/
theorem eval_iterateComp (f : R[X]) (n : ℕ) (x : R) :
    (iterateComp f n).eval x = (fun y => f.eval y)^[n] x := by
  rw [iterateComp, iterate_comp_eval, eval_X]

/-- The chain rule for formal derivatives of composite polynomials:
`(f^{∘n})'(x) = ∏_{j < n} f'(f^j(x))`. -/
theorem eval_derivative_iterateComp (f : R[X]) (n : ℕ) (x : R) :
    (derivative (iterateComp f n)).eval x =
      ∏ j ∈ Finset.range n, (derivative f).eval ((fun y => f.eval y)^[j] x) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [iterateComp_zero]
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [iterateComp_succ, derivative_comp, eval_mul, ih, eval_comp, eval_iterateComp,
      Finset.prod_range_succ]

/-- The chain rule split after `m` steps:
`(f^{∘(m+p)})'(x) = (f^{∘m})'(x) · (f^{∘p})'(f^m(x))`. -/
theorem eval_derivative_iterateComp_add (f : R[X]) (m p : ℕ) (x : R) :
    (derivative (iterateComp f (m + p))).eval x =
      (derivative (iterateComp f m)).eval x *
        (derivative (iterateComp f p)).eval ((fun y => f.eval y)^[m] x) := by
  rw [eval_derivative_iterateComp, eval_derivative_iterateComp, eval_derivative_iterateComp,
    Finset.prod_range_add]
  congr 1
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
  rw [add_comm m j, Function.iterate_add_apply]

/-- A root at which the derivative is nonzero is a simple root. -/
theorem rootMultiplicity_eq_one {Q : R[X]} {x : R} (hx : Q.IsRoot x)
    (hd : (derivative Q).eval x ≠ 0) : Q.rootMultiplicity x = 1 := by
  have hQ : Q ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    apply hd
    rw [derivative_zero, eval_zero]
  have h1 := (rootMultiplicity_pos hQ).mpr hx
  have h2 : ¬ 1 < Q.rootMultiplicity x := fun h =>
    hd ((one_lt_rootMultiplicity_iff_isRoot hQ).mp h).2.eq_zero
  omega

end Chain

/-! ### Multipliers of `F = q⁻¹ P` -/

section Hahn

variable {Γ k : Type*} [AddCommGroup Γ] [LinearOrder Γ] [IsOrderedAddMonoid Γ] [Field k]

local notation "𝒪" => nonnegativeSubring Γ k

/-- The polynomial `F = q⁻¹ P` over `K = k⟦Γ⟧`, for `P ∈ 𝒪[X]`. -/
def forwardPoly (P : Polynomial 𝒪) (q : k⟦Γ⟧) : k⟦Γ⟧[X] :=
  C q⁻¹ * P.map (nonnegativeSubring Γ k).subtype

theorem eval_forwardPoly (P : Polynomial 𝒪) (q x : k⟦Γ⟧) :
    (forwardPoly P q).eval x = forwardMap P q x := by
  rw [forwardPoly, eval_mul, eval_C]
  rfl

theorem eval_forwardPoly_fun (P : Polynomial 𝒪) (q : k⟦Γ⟧) :
    (fun y => (forwardPoly P q).eval y) = forwardMap P q :=
  funext (eval_forwardPoly P q)

/-- The `n`-fold composite polynomial `Fⁿ` of `F = q⁻¹ P`. -/
def iteratePoly (P : Polynomial 𝒪) (q : k⟦Γ⟧) (n : ℕ) : k⟦Γ⟧[X] :=
  iterateComp (forwardPoly P q) n

/-- `Fⁿ(x)`, computed from the composite polynomial, is the `n`-th iterate of `F` at `x`. -/
theorem eval_iteratePoly (P : Polynomial 𝒪) (q : k⟦Γ⟧) (n : ℕ) (x : k⟦Γ⟧) :
    (iteratePoly P q n).eval x = (forwardMap P q)^[n] x := by
  rw [iteratePoly, eval_iterateComp, eval_forwardPoly_fun]

/-- The chain rule for `Fⁿ`: `(Fⁿ)'(x) = ∏_{j < n} F'(F^j(x))`. -/
theorem eval_derivative_iteratePoly (P : Polynomial 𝒪) (q : k⟦Γ⟧) (n : ℕ) (x : k⟦Γ⟧) :
    (derivative (iteratePoly P q n)).eval x =
      ∏ j ∈ Finset.range n, (derivative (forwardPoly P q)).eval ((forwardMap P q)^[j] x) := by
  rw [iteratePoly, eval_derivative_iterateComp, eval_forwardPoly_fun]

/-- `(F^{m+p})'(x) = (F^m)'(x) · (F^p)'(F^m(x))`. -/
theorem eval_derivative_iteratePoly_add (P : Polynomial 𝒪) (q : k⟦Γ⟧) (m p : ℕ)
    (x : k⟦Γ⟧) :
    (derivative (iteratePoly P q (m + p))).eval x =
      (derivative (iteratePoly P q m)).eval x *
        (derivative (iteratePoly P q p)).eval ((forwardMap P q)^[m] x) := by
  rw [← eval_forwardPoly_fun]
  exact eval_derivative_iterateComp_add _ m p x

/-- The key step of `epd:prop:multiplier`: at `y ∈ 𝒪` where the residue derivative `P̄'(st y)`
is nonzero, the multiplier `F'(y) = q⁻¹ P'(y)` has valuation exactly `-κ`, `κ = v(q)`. -/
theorem orderTop_eval_derivative_forwardPoly (P : Polynomial 𝒪) {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ}
    (hq : q.orderTop = κ) {y : 𝒪}
    (hy : (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).derivative.eval (standardPart Γ k y) ≠ 0) :
    ((derivative (forwardPoly P q)).eval (y : k⟦Γ⟧)).orderTop = ((-κ : Γ) : WithTop Γ) := by
  have hst : standardPart Γ k (P.derivative.eval y) ≠ 0 := by
    rwa [← eval_map_apply, ← derivative_map]
  have h : (derivative (forwardPoly P q)).eval (y : k⟦Γ⟧) =
      q⁻¹ * ((P.derivative.eval y : 𝒪) : k⟦Γ⟧) := by
    rw [forwardPoly, derivative_C_mul, eval_mul, eval_C, derivative_map]
    congr 1
    exact eval_map_apply (p := P.derivative) (f := (nonnegativeSubring Γ k).subtype) y
  rw [h, _root_.HahnSeries.orderTop_mul, Surreal.ScaleIdeal.orderTop_inv, hq,
    orderTop_eq_zero_of_standardPart_ne_zero hst, add_zero,
    WithTop.LinearOrderedAddCommGroup.coe_neg]

/-- The itinerary step of the source: if `y ∈ 𝒪` and `F(y) ∈ 𝒪` with `v(q) = κ > 0`, then
`P(y) = q F(y) ∈ 𝔪`, so the residue `st y` is a root of `P̄`. -/
theorem isRoot_map_standardPart (P : Polynomial 𝒪) {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ)
    (hκ : 0 < κ) {y : 𝒪} (hFy : forwardMap P q y ∈ 𝒪) :
    (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).IsRoot (standardPart Γ k y) := by
  have hq0 : q ≠ 0 := Surreal.ScaleIdeal.ne_zero_of_orderTop_eq hq
  have hP : ((P.eval y : 𝒪) : k⟦Γ⟧) = q * forwardMap P q y := by
    rw [forwardMap_coe, mul_inv_cancel_left₀ hq0]
  have hpos : 0 < ((P.eval y : 𝒪) : k⟦Γ⟧).orderTop := by
    rw [hP, _root_.HahnSeries.orderTop_mul, hq]
    exact lt_add_of_lt_of_nonneg (WithTop.coe_lt_coe.mpr hκ) ((mem_nonnegativeSubring _).mp hFy)
  rw [IsRoot.def, eval_map_apply]
  exact standardPart_eq_zero_of_orderTop_pos hpos

/-- `v(F'(y)) = -κ` at every `y ∈ 𝒪` with `F(y) ∈ 𝒪`, when every residue root of `P` is
simple and `v(q) = κ > 0`. -/
theorem orderTop_eval_derivative_forwardPoly_of_mem {P : Polynomial 𝒪}
    (hP : ∀ z : k, (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).IsRoot z →
      (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).derivative.eval z ≠ 0)
    {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ) (hκ : 0 < κ) {y : k⟦Γ⟧} (hy : y ∈ 𝒪)
    (hFy : forwardMap P q y ∈ 𝒪) :
    ((derivative (forwardPoly P q)).eval y).orderTop = ((-κ : Γ) : WithTop Γ) :=
  orderTop_eval_derivative_forwardPoly (y := ⟨y, hy⟩) P hq
    (hP _ (isRoot_map_standardPart (y := ⟨y, hy⟩) P hq hκ hFy))

/-- A finite product of factors of valuation `g` has valuation `n g`. -/
theorem orderTop_prod_range {f : ℕ → k⟦Γ⟧} {g : Γ} {n : ℕ}
    (h : ∀ j < n, (f j).orderTop = g) :
    (∏ j ∈ Finset.range n, f j).orderTop = ((n • g : Γ) : WithTop Γ) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [Finset.prod_range_succ, _root_.HahnSeries.orderTop_mul, ih fun j hj => h j (by omega),
      h n (by omega), succ_nsmul, WithTop.coe_add]

/-- The integral nonescaping set `B_int(F)` is forward invariant. -/
theorem iterate_mem_integralLocus {f : k⟦Γ⟧ → k⟦Γ⟧} {x : k⟦Γ⟧}
    (hx : x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) f) (m : ℕ) :
    f^[m] x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) f := by
  rw [mem_integralLocus_hahn] at hx ⊢
  intro j
  rw [← Function.iterate_add_apply]
  exact hx (j + m)

/-- `epd:prop:multiplier`, clause (1), for any `P ∈ 𝒪[X]` whose residue roots are all simple and
`v(q) = κ > 0`: for `x ∈ B_int(F)` and every `n` (including `n = 0`), `v((Fⁿ)'(x)) = -nκ`. -/
theorem orderTop_eval_derivative_iteratePoly {P : Polynomial 𝒪}
    (hP : ∀ z : k, (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).IsRoot z →
      (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).derivative.eval z ≠ 0)
    {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ) (hκ : 0 < κ) {x : k⟦Γ⟧}
    (hx : x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) (forwardMap P q)) (n : ℕ) :
    ((derivative (iteratePoly P q n)).eval x).orderTop = ((-(n • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ) := by
  rw [mem_integralLocus_hahn] at hx
  have h : ∀ j < n, ((derivative (forwardPoly P q)).eval ((forwardMap P q)^[j] x)).orderTop =
      ((-κ : Γ) : WithTop Γ) := fun j _ =>
    orderTop_eval_derivative_forwardPoly_of_mem hP hq hκ (hx j) (by
      rw [← Function.iterate_succ_apply' (forwardMap P q) j x]
      exact hx (j + 1))
  rw [eval_derivative_iteratePoly, orderTop_prod_range h, smul_neg]

/-- A root of `F^{m+p}(X) - F^m(X)` satisfies `F^{m+p}(x) = F^m(x)`. -/
theorem iterate_eq_of_isRoot {P : Polynomial 𝒪} {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {m p : ℕ} {x : k⟦Γ⟧}
    (hx : (iteratePoly P q (m + p) - iteratePoly P q m).IsRoot x) :
    (forwardMap P q)^[m + p] x = (forwardMap P q)^[m] x := by
  rwa [IsRoot.def, eval_sub, eval_iteratePoly, eval_iteratePoly, sub_eq_zero] at hx

/-- Preperiodic points lie in `B_int(F)`: if `F^{m+p}(x) = F^m(x)` with `p ≥ 1`, every iterate
`y = F^n(x)` also satisfies `F^{m+p}(y) = F^m(y)`, which the escape step forbids when
`v(y) < 0`. This needs `deg P ≥ 2` and a unit leading coefficient. -/
theorem mem_integralLocus_of_iterate_eq {P : Polynomial 𝒪} (hdeg : 2 ≤ P.natDegree)
    (hlead : IsUnit P.leadingCoeff) {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ) (hκ : 0 < κ)
    {m p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) {x : k⟦Γ⟧}
    (hx : (forwardMap P q)^[m + p] x = (forwardMap P q)^[m] x) :
    x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) (forwardMap P q) := by
  have hE := isExpanding_hahn hdeg hlead hq hκ
  rw [forwardMap_eq] at hx ⊢
  rw [mem_integralLocus]
  intro n
  by_contra hn
  set F := Surreal.ValuedIteration.expandingMap q (P.map (nonnegativeSubring Γ k).subtype)
  have h : F^[m + p] (F^[n] x) = F^[m] (F^[n] x) := by
    rw [(Function.Commute.iterate_iterate_self F (m + p) n).eq x, hx,
      (Function.Commute.iterate_iterate_self F n m).eq x]
  exact iterate_add_ne_of_neg hE (not_le.mp hn) m hp h

/-- `epd:prop:multiplier`, clause (2), valuation: at every `x ∈ B_int(F)`, whether or not it is
a root, the derivative of `F^{m+p}(X) - F^m(X)` factors as `(F^m)'(x) ((F^p)'(F^m(x)) - 1)` and
has valuation `-(m + p)κ`, for `p ≥ 1`. -/
theorem orderTop_eval_derivative_preperiodic {P : Polynomial 𝒪}
    (hP : ∀ z : k, (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).IsRoot z →
      (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).derivative.eval z ≠ 0)
    {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ) (hκ : 0 < κ) {m p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) {x : k⟦Γ⟧}
    (hx : x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) (forwardMap P q)) :
    ((derivative (iteratePoly P q (m + p) - iteratePoly P q m)).eval x).orderTop =
      ((-((m + p) • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ) := by
  have hfac : (derivative (iteratePoly P q (m + p) - iteratePoly P q m)).eval x =
      (derivative (iteratePoly P q m)).eval x *
        ((derivative (iteratePoly P q p)).eval ((forwardMap P q)^[m] x) - 1) := by
    rw [derivative_sub, eval_sub, eval_derivative_iteratePoly_add, mul_sub, mul_one]
  have hm := orderTop_eval_derivative_iteratePoly hP hq hκ hx m
  have hpk := orderTop_eval_derivative_iteratePoly hP hq hκ (iterate_mem_integralLocus hx m) p
  have hneg : ((-(p • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ) < 0 :=
    WithTop.coe_lt_coe.mpr (neg_lt_zero.mpr (nsmul_pos hκ hp.ne'))
  have hsub : ((derivative (iteratePoly P q p)).eval ((forwardMap P q)^[m] x) - 1).orderTop =
      ((-(p • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ) := by
    rw [_root_.HahnSeries.orderTop_sub (by rw [hpk, _root_.HahnSeries.orderTop_one]; exact hneg),
      hpk]
  rw [hfac, _root_.HahnSeries.orderTop_mul, hm, hsub, ← WithTop.coe_add, add_nsmul, neg_add]

/-- A root of a polynomial over `K` at which the derivative has finite valuation is simple. -/
theorem rootMultiplicity_eq_one_of_orderTop {Q : k⟦Γ⟧[X]} {x : k⟦Γ⟧} (hx : Q.IsRoot x)
    {g : Γ} (hd : ((derivative Q).eval x).orderTop = g) : Q.rootMultiplicity x = 1 :=
  rootMultiplicity_eq_one hx
    (_root_.HahnSeries.orderTop_ne_top.mp (by rw [hd]; exact WithTop.coe_ne_top))

/-- `epd:prop:multiplier`, clause (2), for any `P ∈ 𝒪[X]` of degree at least two with unit
leading coefficient and simple residue roots, and `v(q) = κ > 0`: every root `x ∈ K` of
`F^{m+p}(X) - F^m(X)` with `p ≥ 1` lies in `B_int(F)`, the derivative of that polynomial at `x`
has valuation `-(m + p)κ`, and the root is simple. Only roots in `K` are addressed; splitting
over `K` is part of `epd:thm:periodic`. -/
theorem preperiodic_root {P : Polynomial 𝒪} (hdeg : 2 ≤ P.natDegree)
    (hlead : IsUnit P.leadingCoeff)
    (hP : ∀ z : k, (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).IsRoot z →
      (P.map (standardPart Γ k)).derivative.eval z ≠ 0)
    {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ) (hκ : 0 < κ) {m p : ℕ} (hp : 0 < p) {x : k⟦Γ⟧}
    (hx : (iteratePoly P q (m + p) - iteratePoly P q m).IsRoot x) :
    x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) (forwardMap P q) ∧
      ((derivative (iteratePoly P q (m + p) - iteratePoly P q m)).eval x).orderTop =
        ((-((m + p) • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ) ∧
      (iteratePoly P q (m + p) - iteratePoly P q m).rootMultiplicity x = 1 := by
  have hB := mem_integralLocus_of_iterate_eq hdeg hlead hq hκ hp (iterate_eq_of_isRoot hx)
  have hv := orderTop_eval_derivative_preperiodic (m := m) hP hq hκ hp hB
  exact ⟨hB, hv, rootMultiplicity_eq_one_of_orderTop hx hv⟩

/-! ### The family `epd:eq:polynomial` -/

/-- Every root of `P₀ = a ∏ (X - c_i)` with `a ≠ 0` is one of the `c_i`. -/
theorem exists_eq_of_isRoot_residuePolynomial {d : ℕ} {a : k} (ha : a ≠ 0) {c : Fin d → k}
    {z : k} (hz : (residuePolynomial a c).IsRoot z) : ∃ i, c i = z := by
  rw [IsRoot.def, residuePolynomial, eval_mul, eval_C, eval_prod, mul_eq_zero] at hz
  rcases hz with h | h
  · exact absurd h ha
  · obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := Finset.prod_eq_zero_iff.mp h
    rw [eval_sub, eval_X, eval_C, sub_eq_zero] at hi
    exact ⟨i, hi.symm⟩

/-- Every residue root of the polynomial of `epd:eq:polynomial` is simple. -/
theorem simpleRoots_perturbedPolynomial {d : ℕ} {a : k} (ha : a ≠ 0) {c : Fin d → k}
    (hc : Function.Injective c) {e : Fin (d + 1) → 𝒪}
    (he : ∀ j, 0 < ((e j : 𝒪) : k⟦Γ⟧).orderTop) (z : k)
    (hz : ((perturbedPolynomial a c e).map (standardPart Γ k)).IsRoot z) :
    ((perturbedPolynomial a c e).map (standardPart Γ k)).derivative.eval z ≠ 0 := by
  rw [map_perturbedPolynomial a c he] at hz ⊢
  obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_of_isRoot_residuePolynomial ha hz
  exact eval_derivative_residuePolynomial_ne_zero ha hc i

/-- `epd:prop:multiplier`, clause (1), for the family `epd:eq:polynomial` over `K = k⟦Γ⟧`:
`P = a ∏ (X - c_i) + ∑_{j ≤ d} e_j X^j` with `a ≠ 0`, distinct `c_i`, `e_j ∈ 𝔪`, and
`q ∈ 𝔪 \ {0}` with `κ = v(q)`. For `x ∈ B_int(F)` and every `n`, `v((Fⁿ)'(x)) = -nκ`, where
`Fⁿ` is the composite polynomial. The hypothesis `d ≥ 2` is not needed here. -/
theorem multiplier_integral {d : ℕ} {a : k} (ha : a ≠ 0) {c : Fin d → k}
    (hc : Function.Injective c) {e : Fin (d + 1) → 𝒪}
    (he : ∀ j, 0 < ((e j : 𝒪) : k⟦Γ⟧).orderTop) {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ)
    (hκ : 0 < κ) {x : k⟦Γ⟧}
    (hx : x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) (forwardMap (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q)) (n : ℕ) :
    ((derivative (iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q n)).eval x).orderTop =
      ((-(n • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ) :=
  orderTop_eval_derivative_iteratePoly (simpleRoots_perturbedPolynomial ha hc he) hq hκ hx n

/-- `epd:prop:multiplier` for the family `epd:eq:polynomial` over `K = k⟦Γ⟧`, with `d ≥ 2`,
`a ≠ 0`, distinct `c_i`, `e_j ∈ 𝔪`, `q ∈ 𝔪 \ {0}` and `κ = v(q)`:
(1) for `x ∈ B_int(F)` and every `n` (in particular `n ≥ 1`, and also `n = 0`),
`v((Fⁿ)'(x)) = -nκ`;
(2) for `m ≥ 0`, `p ≥ 1` and every root `x ∈ K` of `F^{m+p}(X) - F^m(X)`, the root lies in
`B_int(F)`, the derivative of that polynomial at `x` has valuation `-(m + p)κ`, and the root is
simple. Clause (2) concerns roots lying in `K`; that the polynomial splits over `K` with
`d^{m+p}` distinct roots is `epd:thm:periodic`, which is not formalized here. -/
theorem multiplier {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) {a : k} (ha : a ≠ 0) {c : Fin d → k}
    (hc : Function.Injective c) {e : Fin (d + 1) → 𝒪}
    (he : ∀ j, 0 < ((e j : 𝒪) : k⟦Γ⟧).orderTop) {q : k⟦Γ⟧} {κ : Γ} (hq : q.orderTop = κ)
    (hκ : 0 < κ) :
    (∀ x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) (forwardMap (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q), ∀ n : ℕ,
      ((derivative (iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q n)).eval x).orderTop =
        ((-(n • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ)) ∧
    (∀ m p : ℕ, 0 < p → ∀ x : k⟦Γ⟧,
      (iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q (m + p) -
          iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q m).IsRoot x →
        x ∈ integralLocus (addVal Γ k) (forwardMap (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q) ∧
        ((derivative (iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q (m + p) -
            iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q m)).eval x).orderTop =
          ((-((m + p) • κ) : Γ) : WithTop Γ) ∧
        (iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q (m + p) -
          iteratePoly (perturbedPolynomial a c e) q m).rootMultiplicity x = 1) :=
  ⟨fun _ hx n => multiplier_integral ha hc he hq hκ hx n, fun _ _ hp _ hx =>
    preperiodic_root (by rwa [natDegree_perturbedPolynomial ha c he])
      (isUnit_leadingCoeff_perturbedPolynomial ha c he)
      (simpleRoots_perturbedPolynomial ha hc he) hq hκ hp hx⟩

end Hahn

/-! ### Finite-parameter Hahn evaluation -/

section Evaluation

variable {Γ k σ τ : Type*} [AddCommGroup Γ] [LinearOrder Γ] [IsOrderedAddMonoid Γ] [Field k]
  [Fintype σ] [Fintype τ]

/-- The ideal clause of `epd:lem:evaluation`: if a formal series lies in the ideal generated by
the variables `Z_j`, `j ∈ J`, then its evaluation at `x ∈ 𝔪^σ` lies in the ideal
`(x_j : j ∈ J) 𝒪` of the integral ring. -/
theorem mvEvaluateNonnegative_mem_span (x : σ → k⟦Γ⟧) (hx : ∀ i, 0 < (x i).orderTop)
    (J : Set σ) {A : MvPowerSeries σ k} (hA : A ∈ Ideal.span (MvPowerSeries.X '' J)) :
    mvEvaluateNonnegative x hx A ∈
      Ideal.span ((fun j => (⟨x j, (mem_nonnegativeSubring _).mpr (hx j).le⟩ :
        nonnegativeSubring Γ k)) '' J) := by
  have hX : (fun j => mvEvaluateNonnegative x hx (MvPowerSeries.X j)) =
      fun j => (⟨x j, (mem_nonnegativeSubring _).mpr (hx j).le⟩ : nonnegativeSubring Γ k) :=
    funext fun j => Subtype.ext (mvEvaluate_X x hx j)
  have h := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (mvEvaluateNonnegative x hx) hA
  rwa [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_image, hX] at h

/-- `epd:lem:evaluation`, for finitely many parameters `x : σ → K` in `𝔪` (the source's `a_j`;
zero allowed). The evaluation `A ↦ A(x)` is the `k`-algebra homomorphism `mvEvaluate x hx`; that
clause is carried by its type, not by a conjunct below. (i) The family `A_d x^d` is strongly
summable with sum `A(x)`, which is the well-defined strong evaluation. (ii) `A(x) ∈ 𝒪`.
(iii) The support of `A(x)` lies in the additive monoid generated by `⋃_j supp(x_j)`.
(iv) Evaluation respects formal substitution by series `B_i` with zero constant term, whose
evaluations lie in `𝔪`. (v) If `A` lies in the ideal `(Z_j : j ∈ J)`, then `A(x)` lies in
`(x_j : j ∈ J) 𝒪`. -/
theorem evaluation (x : σ → k⟦Γ⟧) (hx : ∀ i, 0 < (x i).orderTop) :
    (∀ A : MvPowerSeries σ k, ∃ s : SummableFamily Γ k (σ →₀ ℕ),
      (∀ d, s d = MvPowerSeries.coeff d A • ∏ i, x i ^ d i) ∧ s.hsum = mvEvaluate x hx A) ∧
    (∀ A : MvPowerSeries σ k, mvEvaluate x hx A ∈ nonnegativeSubring Γ k) ∧
    (∀ A : MvPowerSeries σ k,
      (mvEvaluate x hx A).support ⊆ AddSubmonoid.closure (⋃ i, (x i).support)) ∧
    (∀ (A : MvPowerSeries τ k) (B : τ → MvPowerSeries σ k)
      (hB : ∀ i, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (B i) = 0),
      (∀ i, 0 < (mvEvaluate x hx (B i)).orderTop) ∧
      mvEvaluate x hx (MvPowerSeries.subst B A) =
        mvEvaluate (fun i => mvEvaluate x hx (B i))
          (fun i => orderTop_mvEvaluate_pos_of_constantCoeff_zero x hx (B i) (hB i)) A) ∧
    (∀ (J : Set σ) (A : MvPowerSeries σ k), A ∈ Ideal.span (MvPowerSeries.X '' J) →
      mvEvaluateNonnegative x hx A ∈
        Ideal.span ((fun j => (⟨x j, (mem_nonnegativeSubring _).mpr (hx j).le⟩ :
          nonnegativeSubring Γ k)) '' J)) :=
  ⟨fun A => ⟨mvEvaluationFamily x hx A, mvEvaluationFamily_apply x hx A, rfl⟩,
    fun A => (mem_nonnegativeSubring _).mpr (orderTop_mvEvaluate_nonneg x hx A),
    support_mvEvaluate_subset_closure x hx,
    fun A B hB => ⟨fun i => orderTop_mvEvaluate_pos_of_constantCoeff_zero x hx (B i) (hB i),
      mvEvaluate_subst x hx A B hB⟩,
    fun J _ hA => mvEvaluateNonnegative_mem_span x hx J hA⟩

end Evaluation

end

end Surreal.ExpandingMultipliers
